  "provider_query": "PEP 703 page that proposes making the CPython GIL optional",
  "answer": "**Primary page:** [PEP 703 – Making the Global Interpreter Lock Optional in CPython](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)\n\n1. **[PEP 703 (peps.python.org)](https://peps.python.org/pep-0703/)** — Official PEP by Sam Gross (sponsor: Łukasz Langa). Proposes a `--disable-gil` build so CPython can run without the GIL (ABI tag includes `t`). Status: **Final** (historical; accepted for 3.13; canonical docs now point at free-threading support).\n\n2. **[Steering Council acceptance (Discussions)](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython-acceptance/37075)** — 24 Oct 2023 acceptance with a gradual three-phase rollout (experimental → supported but not default → possibly default later), and the term “free-threaded.”\n\n3. **[Steering Council intent-to-accept notice](https://discuss.python.org/t/a-steering-council-notice-about-pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional-in-cpython/30474)** — July 2023 notice of intent to accept and the staged plan (experimental in 3.13).\n\n4. **[PEP 779 – Criteria for supported status for free-threaded Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0779/)** — Follow-on PEP that set Phase II criteria; free-threaded builds became officially supported in 3.14 (still not the default).\n\n5. **[GitHub PR #2955 (python/peps)](https://github.com/python/peps/pull/2955)** — Original submission of PEP 703 by `colesbury` (merged Jan 2023).\n\n6. **[Original Discourse thread](https://discuss.python.org/t/pep-703-making-the-global-interpreter-lock-optional/22606)** — Early discussion of the proposal (including the `--disable-gil` configure flag).\n\n7. **[What is PEP 703? (pydevtools handbook)](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/explanation/what-is-pep-703.md)** — Short explainer: separate free-threaded build, `t` ABI, experimental in 3.13 and supported in 3.14, GIL still default.\n\n8. **[PEP 805 – Safe Parallel Python](https://peps.python.org/pep-0805/)** — Later draft that builds on PEP 703 and addresses race-safety once the GIL is optional.",
